# Face Yourself may target its own controller: Bot1 copies its own Savannah Lions while controlling Ajani Resolute, so at
# the beginning of the end step the intervening "if you don't control a planeswalker" is false (CR 603.4) and the copy
# stays. The sacrifice ability is part of the copy for good (CR 707.9b): on T4 Bot2's Grizzly Bears and Llanowar Elves
# attack and kill Ajani (2 + 1 damage against 2 loyalty), and at that turn's end step, with no planeswalker, the copy is
# sacrificed while the original Lions stays.
[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus x4
Ajani Resolute
Savannah Lions
Face Yourself
Plains x10
[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Grizzly Bears
Llanowar Elves
Forest x4
Forest x10
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Ajani Resolute.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Savannah Lions.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Face Yourself.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Savannah Lions#2.Keywords = Haste
[T3 Bot1.End]
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Ajani Resolute; Savannah Lions; Savannah Lions
Bot2.Attack(Grizzly Bears > Bot1.Battlefield.Ajani Resolute; Llanowar Elves > Bot1.Battlefield.Ajani Resolute)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Savannah Lions
Bot1.Graveyard = Ajani Resolute; Face Yourself; Black Lotus; Black Lotus; Black Lotus; Black Lotus
